SPDX-License-Identifier and copyright headers:

  kernels/triton_attn.py                  <- vllm/v1/attention/backends/triton_attn.py
  kernels/triton_unified_attention.py     <- vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention.py
  kernels/triton_attention_helpers.py     <- vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_attention_helpers.py
  kernels/vocab_parallel_embedding.py     <- vllm/model_executor/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py
  kernels/modular_kernel.py               <- vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/modular_kernel.py
  kernels/triton_moe.py                   <- vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/triton_moe.py
  kernels/fused_moe.py                    <- vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py

  kernels/fused_act_quant.py              new file; follows the structure of vLLM's
                                          silu_and_mul_per_block_quant fusion for an activation
                                          and scale layout vLLM does not fuse.

Modifications are gated behind NX_* environment variables; with none set, the files behave as
upstream. Each modification carries an in-file comment stating what it changes and why.

Benchmark harnesses under bench/ invoke `vllm bench serve` from the vLLM image.
